  Rewrite by m0us3r - https://github.com/mym0us3r/Unified-Sysmon-Configs
  Date: 07/24/2026 Friday

  Sysmon Pipe Event rules: 100700 - 100715
  Rewritten for Sysmon Native (Windows 11 24H2+)
  Provider: Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon
  EID 17/18: PipeEvent (Created/Connected) - C2 named pipe detection
  MITRE ATT&CK v15 aligned

  ESCAPING REFERENCE (critical):
    Wazuh decoder doubles backslashes in Windows paths.
    Stored internally: C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe (double backslash)
    PCRE2 to match \\: use \\\\
    Rule: path separators -> \\\\ | regex meta (\s \d \b \.) -> \\

  CONTEXT:
    Named pipes are Cobalt Strike's default inter-process/lateral-
    movement mechanism (SMB beacon). sysmon-native.xml already filters
    EID 17/18 down to only known-bad default pipe name patterns
    (msagent_, MSSE-, psexec, postex_, status_) - meaning every event
    that reaches this anchor already matched a suspicious pattern at
    the endpoint. This file's job is to alert on it, not re-filter it.

  KNOWN LIMITATION:
    This only catches DEFAULT Cobalt Strike pipe names. Any operator
    using a custom Malleable C2 profile with a renamed pipe evades this
    entirely - the pipe name list is not a substitute for behavioral
    detection elsewhere in this ruleset (e.g. 0870 CreateRemoteThread).

  MIGRATION NOTES:
    ANCHORS: if_group>sysmon_event_17 (EID 17, pipe created) and
    if_group>sysmon_event_18 (EID 18, pipe connected), both assigned
    in 0595-win-sysmon_rules.xml (rules 61645/61646). Two separate
    anchors are used deliberately - if_group's documented behavior is
    a single group name per tag, not a comma-separated list like
    if_sid, so one anchor cannot safely cover both event types.
    This is a NEW file - not yet field-tested. Validate with
    wazuh-analysisd -t and a live test before treating as
    production-confirmed.
-->

<group name="sysmon,sysmon_eid17_18,windows,">

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       BASE ANCHOR - EID 17 (Pipe Created)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rule id="100700" level="12">
    <if_group>sysmon_event_17</if_group>
    <field name="win.system.providerName">^Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon$</field>
    <description>CRITICAL: Known C2 named pipe created - $(win.eventdata.pipeName) by $(win.eventdata.image)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1071.001</id>
      <id>T1021.002</id>
    </mitre>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
  </rule>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       BASE ANCHOR - EID 18 (Pipe Connected)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rule id="100701" level="12">
    <if_group>sysmon_event_18</if_group>
    <field name="win.system.providerName">^Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon$</field>
    <description>CRITICAL: Connection to known C2 named pipe - $(win.eventdata.pipeName) by $(win.eventdata.image)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1071.001</id>
      <id>T1021.002</id>
    </mitre>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
  </rule>

</group>
